  "note": "text_layer was null; every cell was read from the image, and the whole table was re-read at native resolution column by column because the 5d and 5f headings are printed close together and the downscaled view of that band is ambiguous. This is the continuation of Table 2.6 from the previous page: table_continues_from_previous is true and the header row IS reprinted at the top of this page, so repeated_header is true and the header is given. The table prints no configuration strings and no superscripts: each subshell is its own column and each cell holds the bare occupancy number, so cells are transcribed as the plain digits printed and an unoccupied subshell is an empty cell (\"\"). The header is read as 20 columns (Element, Z and the 18 subshell headings) although the printed rules group the headings into seven boxed bands (1s | 2s 2p | 3s 3p 3d | 4s 4p 4d 4f | 5s 5p 5d 5f | 6s 6p 6d | 7s) and put Element and Z in one box; the subshell letters are printed in italic. One horizontal rule inside the table, between Rn (86) and Fr (87), separates the two period blocks; it is structural only and no blank row was added for it. AS PRINTED, NOT CORRECTED: four rows do not add up to their own Z because of the 5f value printed on them - Rf 104 prints 5f 10 (sums to 100), Db 105 prints 5f 11 (sums to 102), Sg 106 prints 5f 12 (sums to 104) and Bh 107 prints 5f 13 (sums to 106), where the surrounding rows Lr 103, Hs 108, Mt 109 and Ds 110 all print 5f 14 and do add up. These four cells were checked at native resolution and the digits 10, 11, 12 and 13 are what the page prints; they are copied unchanged rather than corrected to 14. Every other row sums exactly to its Z. EXCLUDED as outside target_box_in_crop (box lower edge y=1783): the table's final printed data row, which reads Rg** | 111 | 1s 2 | 2s 2 | 2p 6 | 3s 2 | 3p 6 | 3d 10 | 4s 2 | 4p 6 | 4d 10 | 4f 14 | 5s 2 | 5p 6 | 5d 10 | 5f 14 | 6s 2 | 6p 6 | 6d 10 | 7s 1, whose glyphs begin at y=1782 and run below the 